{{project}}
{{'=' * len(project)}}

Installation and Setup
======================

Install ``{{project}}`` in editable mode with pip::

    $ cd {{project}}
    $ python -m pip install -e '.[development]'

Run the test suite::

    $ python -m pytest

{{if sqlalchemy}}
Create the project database for the generated SQLAlchemy models::

    $ gearbox setup-app
{{endif}}

Start the web application::

    $ gearbox serve

While developing you may want the server to reload after changes are saved::

    $ gearbox serve --reload --debug

Then open http://localhost:8080/ and you will be redirected to the demo.

Configuration Profiles and Checks
=================================

Quickstart creates ``development.ini`` for local development and ``test.ini``
for tests; ``test.ini`` references the development configuration. Quickstart
does not generate ``production.ini`` because production configuration is
deployment-specific.

For a compact project check::

    $ gearbox tginfo summary --project . --config development.ini --json
    $ gearbox tginfo routes --project . --config development.ini --json
    $ python -m pytest --collect-only -q

{{if sqlalchemy and migrations}}
Database Migrations
===================

Alembic is included in the development dependencies. Migrations are usually
not needed during ordinary development. To read the current database revision
without changing it, run::

    $ gearbox migrate -c development.ini db_version

Creating a revision, autogenerating a revision, and upgrading a database are
deliberate schema or deployment operations::

    $ gearbox migrate -c development.ini create 'Describe the schema change'
    $ gearbox migrate -c development.ini autogenerate 'Describe the schema change'
    $ gearbox migrate -c development.ini upgrade
{{endif}}

Quickstart also installs optional coding-agent skills into the project-local
``.agents/skills/`` directory. To install them for Claude Code instead, run
``gearbox tgskills --claude`` from the project root; this installs only
``.claude/skills/``. Delete the installed skills directory if you do not use
that assistant.

Generated Demo Code
===================

The quickstart includes a small Kajiki + Bootstrap 5 demo under
``{{package}}.controllers.demo``.
{{if sqlalchemy}}
It also includes a SQLAlchemy ``TodoItem`` model in ``{{package}}.model.todo``
so you can see a database-backed, server-rendered htmx interaction.
{{else}}
This project was created without SQLAlchemy, so the database-backed todo demo
was omitted.
{{endif}}
{{if auth}}
Authentication is enabled, so the demo includes one protected action at
``/demo/protected``.
{{else}}
Authentication is disabled, so protected demo links and actions are omitted.
{{endif}}

When you are ready to build your own application, delete
``{{package}}/controllers/demo.py``, ``{{package}}/model/todo.py`` if present,
and ``{{package}}/templates/demo``. Then change ``RootController.index`` to
redirect or render your own starting page.
